  "observations": [
    "Native2048 scene assembled from four bounded1024 contexts matches whole-frame canonical oracle in every f32 channel bit. Mask partitions only calculate union geometry; all selected pixels enter one joint2048 inference.",
    "Whole selected person mask is 1154x1669, larger than production1024, with1045630 expanded hole pixels. No pixel resampling, 8-bit model input, independent model tiles, shipping pin or cap change.",
    "All18 Auto/Neutral EV(-3,0,+3)/WB(-1000,0,+1000) research grades retain whole-frame known/protected f32 samples exactly. Identity fp16 round-trip max scene error0.001739501953125 at+3EV; no independent ACR pass is implied.",
    "Visual photographic structure check fails: broad textile-like fill tracks the shopper silhouette, with retained rim/bag fragments and no plausible reconstructed market background. Source truth.png means original scene, not hidden-background ground truth. No numerical photographic acceptance score claimed.",
    "Reject larger model admission on this observed challenge; replacing preview quantization/rectangle with exact RAW/person mask did not qualify fill quality.",
    "ORT and reference were separate single-owner Python research processes on shared M5Max128GiB host, four CPU threads. Single runs are neither controlled latency distributions nor16/24/32GiB device proof.",
    "No native UI runtime, saved XMP2048, GPU/live/tile/export,100MPperformance, browser or legal/signing qualification. Native library inputs unchanged; existing Mac build remains current."
  ],
